# Dependencies — no new packages, no silent bumps

## Context

`app/package.json` has zero runtime dependencies and only `typescript`/
`vitest` as devDependencies — intentionally minimal.

## Rule

- Do NOT add any package to `app/package.json` (`dependencies` or
  `devDependencies`) unless the user's request explicitly names the package
  and asks for it to be added.
- Do NOT change the version of an existing dependency (`typescript`,
  `vitest`) unless explicitly asked to.
- This includes state-management libraries (redux/zustand/mobx/jotai),
  utility libraries (lodash/underscore/ramda), and test-tooling alternatives
  (jest/mocha/chai) — the app already has vitest and does not need another.
- If a task seems to need a new package or a version bump to work around an
  error, say so and ask instead of making the change silently.

## How to verify

1. `git diff app/package.json app/package-lock.json` is empty, unless the
   task explicitly requested a dependency change.
2. `cd app && npm test` still runs with the existing `node_modules` (no
   `npm install <new-package>` or `npm install <pkg>@<newversion>` was run as
   part of the task).
3. A manual diff of `app/package.json` shows no new/changed entries under
   `dependencies`/`devDependencies`.